{"title":"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2023 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">2023 AMC 10B #4</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2023 AMC 12B #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Scientific_Form)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Scientific Form)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jackson's paintbrush makes a narrow strip with a width of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/7314f8133d3b925b9ce6598191d153da7ecdd779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> millimeters. Jackson has enough paint to make a strip <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> meters long. How many square centimeters of paper could Jackson cover with paint? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5cc9dccf52d0581cad5f2e4463efa57beb581d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 162,500 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 162.5 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) }1,625 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) }1,625,000 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 16,250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"592\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/7314f8133d3b925b9ce6598191d153da7ecdd779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> millimeters is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/6/8160a33051fc4866eaa8da6dae42a7110ccff735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> centimeters. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> meters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b32623c3d21608acb59f855590c5b920018645a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2500$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> centimeters. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cbcdfd63ac16300037e58f9865d3443f6570668.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.65 \\times 2500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/425b3384f11c233c53ce65d4ee0b47b1e6670728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) 1,625}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~Failure.net\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Scientific_Form.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Scientific_Form)\">Solution 2 (Scientific Form)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Scientific Form)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/7314f8133d3b925b9ce6598191d153da7ecdd779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> millimeters can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/f/bbf19fe90d780e7b619273d875312d5c0c6614ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65 \\times 10^{-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> centimeters. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> meters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d91e01e38359481f0be7ccfc26f190caa71b5910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 \\times 10^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> centimeters. Multiplying out these results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74fd234204ce08a93ec86a48aa73b8e1a736eac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(65 \\times 10^{-2}) \\times (25 \\times 10^{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"21\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/4/ae44e3c93f44174fd871c1afca9460ef7f6dfbf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65 \\times 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> making the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/425b3384f11c233c53ce65d4ee0b47b1e6670728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) 1,625}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~darrenn.cp\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A good way to remember metric conversions is with the phrase <b> \"King Henry Died By Drinking Chocolate Milk\" </b> (Kilo, Hecto, Deka, Basic units, Deci, Centi, Milli). As you read from left to right you divide by 10. So 1 meter (which is a basic unit) is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> millimeters, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> centimeters. \n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:grogg007\">grogg007</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SUnhwbA5_So\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SUnhwbA5_So</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/EuLkw8HFdk4?si=mEwHK_VyAr1h0O1A&amp;t=808\">https://youtu.be/EuLkw8HFdk4?si=mEwHK_VyAr1h0O1A&amp;t=808</a> \n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BZ1zeFvw5hU\">https://youtu.be/BZ1zeFvw5hU</a>\n</p><p><br />\n~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gDnmvcOzxjg?si=cYB6uChy7Ue0UT4L\">https://youtu.be/gDnmvcOzxjg?si=cYB6uChy7Ue0UT4L</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B\" title=\"2023 AMC 10B\">2023 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redi